cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Pockmark Stats Finder: a QGIS plugin for measuring pockmarks from hand-drawn outlines"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Kalski
    given-names: Ramon
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0003-5342-1941"
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-11-20"
# doi: 10.5281/zenodo.0000000
license:
  - MIT
  - GPL-2.0-or-later
repository-code: "https://github.com/RamonKalski/pockmark-stats-finder"
abstract: >-
  A QGIS plugin that measures seafloor pockmarks from outlines drawn by hand on a
  bathymetry grid. For each outline it finds the center and the deepest point near
  the center, and measures size, depth and volume below the rim, shape, direction,
  slopes, the nearest other pockmark, and whether it sits inside another one.
keywords:
  - pockmark
  - bathymetry
  - seafloor
  - QGIS
  - morphometry
